# Line endings.
#
# Every source file in this repo is LF, and it has to stay that way whatever
# machine it is edited on. On Windows a plain `open(path, "w")` or
# `pathlib.write_text()` translates "\n" to "\r\n", so a tool that rewrites a
# whole file silently flips it — which shows up as a diff touching every line
# and buries the three lines that actually changed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes git normalise on commit regardless of what wrote the
# file, so the repository stays LF even when a working tree is not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches the bytes. `text=auto` detects most of these on
# its own; naming them is cheaper than trusting the heuristic on a font.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.avif   binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.eot    binary
*.db     binary
*.7z     binary
*.zip    binary
*.mp3    binary
*.mp4    binary
